# Day 35

## Experiment Title

Testing and Packaging Applications using Maven


## Objective

To understand how Maven performs application testing and packaging during the build lifecycle.


## Theory

Maven provides automated testing and packaging features through its build lifecycle. Testing ensures that the application functions correctly before deployment, while packaging creates executable files such as JAR or WAR files.

Maven automatically executes testing and packaging tasks based on the project configuration defined inside the pom.xml file.


## Requirements

Java Development Kit

Apache Maven

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the Maven project directory.

Execute the Maven testing process for the application.

Observe the testing results generated by Maven.

Run the packaging process to create the application package.

Verify the generated package inside the target directory.


## Output

The application testing process completed successfully.

Maven generated the application package successfully.

The executable package was stored inside the target directory.


## Result

Successfully performed testing and packaging of a Java application using Apache Maven.
